        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ribadire",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ribadire — \"to reiterate, to restate firmly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ribadisco quello che ho detto: io non vengo. I repeat what I said: I am not coming."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Conjugated with -isc-: ribadisco. The first sense is to clinch a nail by bending its point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of ribadire is not settled; EtymDB records the word with no source (EtymDB). Its first sense was \"to clinch a nail by hammering its point flat\", and from there it came to mean to hammer a point home with words."
            }
          ]
        },
